br/docs/getting-started-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#1-install-brok","content":"**macOS / Linux**","locale":"pt-br"},"533":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-25","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#1-install-brok","content":"**Windows (PowerShell)**","locale":"pt-br"},"534":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-26","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#1-install-brok","content":"Both install two programs, `brok` and `brok-agent`, and check their\nchecksums. Open a new terminal and check:","locale":"pt-br"},"535":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-27","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#1-install-brok","content":"**Company laptop blocks the script?** Download `brok-windows-x86_64.exe`\nfrom the brok release\nand `brok-agent-windows-x86_64.exe` from the\nagent release,\nrename them `brok.exe` and `brok-agent.exe`, put both in one folder and add\nthat folder to your `PATH`.","locale":"pt-br"},"536":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-28","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#1-install-brok","content":"**Prefer Cargo?** `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent` (needs a C compiler and\n`protoc`), or `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent --no-default-features` for a\nlighter build with text search only.","locale":"pt-br"},"537":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-29","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"Search works without any LLM. Answers (`brok ask`, `chat`, `review`,\n`commit`) need one. A local model is free, private and works offline.","locale":"pt-br"},"538":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-30","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"**Ollama** (recommended):","locale":"pt-br"},"539":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-31","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| OS      | Install                        |\n| ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Windows | `winget install Ollama.Ollama` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"540":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-32","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| OS    | Install               |\n| ----- | --------------------- |\n| macOS | `brew install ollama` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"541":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-33","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| OS    | Install                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Linux | `curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh \\| sh` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"542":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-34","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"Pick the model for your machine:","locale":"pt-br"},"543":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-35","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| Your machine | Model                | Download                         |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| 8 GB         | `qwen2.5-coder:1.5b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:1.5b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"544":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-36","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| Your machine                          | Model              | Download                       |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 16 GB, no GPU (most business laptops) | `qwen2.5-coder:3b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:3b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"545":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-37","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| Your machine                                                   | Model              | Download                       |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 16 GB with a GPU (6 GB+) or Apple Silicon; 32 GB without a GPU | `qwen2.5-coder:7b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"546":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-38","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"| Your machine                                            | Model               | Download                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| A GPU with 12 GB+, or 32 GB with a GPU or Apple Silicon | `qwen2.5-coder:14b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:14b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"547":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-39","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"Not sure? Skip the pull: `brok init` (next step) measures your machine and\noffers to download the right one.","locale":"pt-br"},"548":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-40","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"Small models (1.5b, 3b) are fine for questions (`ask`, `chat`); reviews and\ncommit messages are much better with 7b or larger. Without a GPU, a 7b\nmodel takes a few minutes per review, which is why the table suggests 3b\nthere.","locale":"pt-br"},"549":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-41","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#2-get-a-local-llm-optional","content":"Prefer a graphical app? LM Studio works too: download a\nmodel, open **Developer / Local Server** and press **Start Server**. More in\nLocal LLM setup.","locale":"pt-br"},"550":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-42","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"Go to your project (one repository, or a folder holding several) and run\n(want a sample project first? clone\nexample-nestjs):","locale":"pt-br"},"551":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-43","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"It walks through six steps and asks before anything big:","locale":"pt-br"},"552":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-44","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step         | What happens                                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1. Workspace | Creates `.brokspace/` with a commented `brok.yml` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"553":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-45","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step     | What happens                                                               |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Agent | Installs `brok-agent`, the helper that tracks changes and talks to the LLM |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"554":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-46","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step               | What happens                                                           |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 3. Semantic search | Downloads the search model once (~140 MB, shared by all your projects) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"555":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-47","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step         | What happens                                                      |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 4. Local LLM | Finds Ollama / LM Studio and picks a model that fits your machine |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"556":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-48","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step     | What happens                                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 5. Index | Indexes your code (functions, classes and sections, not raw text) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"557":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-49","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"| Step             | What happens                                                          |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 6. Coding agents | Connects Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code or Codex (skills + search tool) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"558":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-50","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"Want no questions? `brok init --yes` accepts every recommendation.\nThen check the result:","locale":"pt-br"},"559":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-51","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"Every line is either ✓, or a `!` with the exact command that fixes it.","locale":"pt-br"},"560":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-52","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#3-set-up-your-first-workspace","content":"> Your next project is faster: the search model and your LLM choice are\n> remembered, so `brok init` there takes seconds.","locale":"pt-br"},"561":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-53","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"The first `ask`, `chat`, `review` or `commit` starts brok in the background.\nFrom then on the index follows you: saved files, commits, pulls and branch\nswitches are picked up within seconds.","locale":"pt-br"},"562":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-54","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                      | Run                        |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| Start / stop the background service | `brok start` / `brok stop` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"563":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-55","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                      | Run            |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Restart it after editing `brok.yml` | `brok restart` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"564":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-56","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...       | Run            |\n| -------------------- | -------------- |\n| See what it is doing | `brok logs -f` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"565":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-57","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...      | Run           |\n| ------------------- | ------------- |\n| See what is indexed | `brok status` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"566":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-58","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                          | Run                                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Review only staged changes, or a branch | `brok review --staged` / `brok review --base main` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"567":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-59","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...              | Run                   |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| Just print a commit message | `brok commit --print` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"568":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-60","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                         | Run                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Use a different model for one question | `brok ask -p anthropic \"...\"` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"569":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-61","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                          | Run                                   |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Show whole results, or JSON for scripts | `brok search \"...\" --full` / `--json` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"570":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-62","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to...                 | Run                    |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------- |\n| Rebuild the index from scratch | `brok index --rebuild` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"571":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-63","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"| You want to... | Run                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tab completion | `brok completions bash >> ~/.bashrc` (also zsh, fish, powershell) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"572":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-64","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"**About AI reviews.** With a local 7b model, `brok review` is a quick first\npass: it catches slips you would rather not push, but it also gets things\nwrong (we have seen it invent a missing validation). Read its findings as\nquestions, not verdicts. For a review you want to rely on, use a 14b model\nor a hosted one for that run: `brok review -p anthropic` (see\nConfigure for API keys).","locale":"pt-br"},"573":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-65","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#4-use-it-every-day","content":"Inside `brok chat`: `/skill grill-me` applies a skill to the conversation,\n`/clear` forgets it, `/exit` leaves.","locale":"pt-br"},"574":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-66","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"If you skipped step 6 of `brok init`:","locale":"pt-br"},"575":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-67","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"It detects your agents and, for each one, adds:","locale":"pt-br"},"576":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-68","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"a **search tool** (`brok_search`) through MCP, so the agent finds code by\nmeaning before grepping;","locale":"pt-br"},"577":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-69","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"the **built-in skills**, such as `/ask-brok`, `/grill-me`, `/to-spec`,\n`tdd` and `code-review`.","locale":"pt-br"},"578":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-70","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"| Agent       | Files written                  |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json`, `.claude/skills/` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-4"},"579":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-71","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"| Agent  | Files written                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| Cursor | `.cursor/mcp.json`, `.agents/skills/` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-4"},"580":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-72","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"| Agent             | Files written                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| VS Code / Copilot | `.vscode/mcp.json`, `.agents/skills/` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-4"},"581":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-73","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"| Agent | Files written                                                       |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Codex | `.agents/skills/` (prints the MCP lines for `~/.codex/config.toml`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-4"},"582":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-74","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#5-connect-your-coding-agent","content":"Commit these files and your whole team gets the same setup. In your agent,\nstart with `/ask-brok` and describe what you want to do.","locale":"pt-br"},"583":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-75","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"Everything lives in **`.brokspace/brok.yml`**. Every key is optional and the\ndefaults are sensible. The settings people change most:","locale":"pt-br"},"584":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-76","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"Easier ways to change things:","locale":"pt-br"},"585":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-77","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"| Change                        | Command                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Switch the local LLM or model | `brok setup llm` (or `brok setup llm --provider ollama --model llama3:8b`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-5"},"586":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-78","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"| Change                     | Command             |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Connect more coding agents | `brok setup agents` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-5"},"587":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-79","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"| Change                                   | Command           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| Share the index (Git LFS, S3, R2, MinIO) | `brok setup sync` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-5"},"588":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-80","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"After editing `brok.yml`, run `brok restart`. Every key is explained in\nConfiguration reference.","locale":"pt-br"},"589":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-81","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#6-configure","content":"**API keys** are never written to files: export them in your shell\n(`export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`, or `$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"...\"` in\nPowerShell) and Brokspace reads them when needed. Secrets found in your code\nare removed from the context before anything is sent to an LLM.","locale":"pt-br"},"590":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-82","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#7-skills","content":"A skill is a small, reusable workflow for AI: a `SKILL.md` file with\ninstructions. Brokspace ships 20 of them.","locale":"pt-br"},"591":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-83","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#7-skills","content":"**User-invoked** skills are started by you (type `/name` in your agent, e.g.\n`/grill-me` before a big change). **Model-invoked** skills are picked by the\nagent when the task fits (e.g. `tdd`, `code-review`).","locale":"pt-br"},"592":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-84","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#7-skills","content":"Write your own:","locale":"pt-br"},"593":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-85","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#7-skills","content":"A workspace skill with the same name as a built-in one replaces it, so you\ncan tailor any built-in to your team. More in Skills.","locale":"pt-br"},"594":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-86","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#8-shards","content":"Shards are small programs that react to what happens in your workspace (a\nfile changed, a question was asked) and can publish their own events. The\nagent you installed is one.","locale":"pt-br"},"595":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-87","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#8-shards","content":"Every shard lists the permissions it wants in `shard.json`, and you approve\nthem when installing. Guide: Shards.","locale":"pt-br"},"596":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-88","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"Start with `brok doctor`: it checks everything and prints the fix.","locale":"pt-br"},"597":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-89","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                    | Fix                                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `no answer from the agent` | Start your LLM (open Ollama / LM Studio), then `brok doctor` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"598":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-90","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                       | Fix                                             |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `ollama ... is not installed` | `ollama pull <model>` as shown by `brok doctor` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"599":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-91","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom              | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Answers take minutes | The model runs on your CPU. Normal for 7b on a laptop without a GPU (a review can take 3 to 5 minutes); for faster answers use 3b: `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:3b`, then `brok setup llm --provider ollama --model qwen2.5-coder:3b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"600":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-92","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                   | Fix                                                              |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Search misses recent code | `brok status`; if the daemon is stopped, `brok start` catches up |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"601":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-93","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                                     | Fix                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `another brok process is writing the index` | `brok` is running in the background and already indexes for you; skip `brok index`, or `brok stop` first |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"602":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-94","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                        | Fix                                                |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Results come back as text only | The search model is missing: `brok model download` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"603":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-95","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                            | Fix                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Agent does not show the brok tools | `brok` must be on `PATH`; run `brok setup agents` and restart the agent |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"604":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-96","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                       | Fix                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Odd behavior after an upgrade | `brok restart`; if it persists, `brok index --rebuild` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"605":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-97","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                          | Fix                                                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Windows: errors about long paths | Enable long paths (`brok doctor` shows the command) or use a shorter folder |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-6"},"606":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-98","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#9-troubleshooting","content":"Still stuck? Run `brok logs -n 100` and ask in\nDiscussions, including the\noutput of `brok doctor`.","locale":"pt-br"},"607":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-99","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#10-update-brok","content":"`brok upgrade` downloads the new `brok` and `brok-agent`, checks them\nagainst the release checksums, swaps them in and restarts brok in every\nworkspace where it was running (each workspace's agent is refreshed on\nthat restart). `brok doctor` tells you when a new version is out.","locale":"pt-br"},"608":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-100","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#10-update-brok","content":"Then run `brok skill export` in your workspaces so your coding agents get\nthe updated built-in skills.","locale":"pt-br"},"609":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-101","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#10-update-brok","content":"Installed with Cargo? Upgrade with `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent`.\nComing from brok 0.2.1 or older (no `upgrade` command yet)? Run the install\ncommand from step 1 again, once.","locale":"pt-br"},"610":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-102","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#11-uninstall","content":"Then delete:","locale":"pt-br"},"611":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-103","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#11-uninstall","content":"the `.brokspace/` folder of each workspace (plus `.agents/skills`,\n`.claude/skills` and the MCP files if you no longer want them);","locale":"pt-br"},"612":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-104","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#11-uninstall","content":"the shared model cache: `~/.cache/brokspace` (Linux),\n`~/Library/Caches/brokspace` (macOS), `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\brokspace` (Windows);","locale":"pt-br"},"613":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-105","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#11-uninstall","content":"your defaults: `~/.config/brokspace` (Linux),\n`~/Library/Application Support/brokspace` (macOS), `%APPDATA%\\brokspace`\n(Windows);","locale":"pt-br"},"614":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started-106","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/getting-started#11-uninstall","content":"the `brok` and `brok-agent` programs (`~/.local/bin`, or\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\brok` on Windows; `cargo uninstall brok-cli brok-agent`\nif you used Cargo).","locale":"pt-br"},"615":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","type":"page","content":"Shard Hub (prévia)","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Ecossistema"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","locale":"pt-br"},"616":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"A casa oficial de shards, skills e agentes para o Brokspace.","locale":"pt-br"},"617":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"O Hub está sendo construído. Até ele abrir, instale shards de qualquer\nrepositório git com `brok shard install <url>`.","locale":"pt-br"},"618":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"O Brokspace Hub será o catálogo oficial de shards feitos pelo time do\nBrokspace e, mais tarde, um registro em que qualquer pessoa poderá publicar,\nno espírito do Docker Hub:","locale":"pt-br"},"619":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"**Shards e pacotes de skills oficiais**, revisados e versionados.","locale":"pt-br"},"620":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"**Instalação com um comando** pela CLI e pela Brokspace IDE.","locale":"pt-br"},"621":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"**Permissões às claras:** cada shard lista o que pode ler, escrever,\nexecutar e acessar antes de você instalá-lo.","locale":"pt-br"},"622":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/hub-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/hub","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/hub","content":"Hoje, crie os seus com Shards e\nSkills, começando pelo\ntemplate de shard.","locale":"pt-br"},"623":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"page","content":"Brokspace IDE","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Brokspace IDE"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide","locale":"pt-br"},"624":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide","content":"Uma IDE com o Brokspace embutido, para o modo IDE ao lado da CLI brok.","locale":"pt-br"},"625":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#instalação","content":"Instalação","locale":"pt-br"},"626":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"Seus primeiros minutos","locale":"pt-br"},"627":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#a-visão-brokspace","content":"A visão Brokspace","locale":"pt-br"},"628":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"O agente Brokspace","locale":"pt-br"},"629":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#comandos-e-idiomas","content":"Comandos e idiomas","locale":"pt-br"},"630":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#como-funciona","content":"Como funciona","locale":"pt-br"},"631":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide","content":"A Brokspace IDE é feita sobre o Eclipse Theia,\nentão extensões do VS Code do Open VSX funcionam\nnela. Ela já vem com o `brok` e o `brok-agent` e os coloca no seu `PATH`.","locale":"pt-br"},"632":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#instalação","content":"Na primeira vez, abra com clique direito > **Abrir** enquanto o app ainda\nnão é notarizado.","locale":"pt-br"},"633":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#instalação","content":"Baixe o AppImage ou o `.tar.gz` da\nversão mais recente.","locale":"pt-br"},"634":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#instalação","content":"Baixe `BrokspaceIDE-<versão>-windows-x64-setup.exe` da\nversão mais recente.\nNo SmartScreen, escolha **Mais informações > Executar assim mesmo**\nenquanto o instalador ainda não é assinado.","locale":"pt-br"},"635":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#instalação","content":"A IDE se atualiza sozinha pelo GitHub Releases. Para receber respostas\nescritas você precisa de um LLM: veja LLM local (a\nbusca funciona sem ele).","locale":"pt-br"},"636":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"A janela começa enxuta: Explorer, Busca, Controle de Código-Fonte e Brokspace\nà esquerda, e o **agente Brokspace** fixo à direita. Depuração, Testes e\nExtensões ficam a um atalho de distância.","locale":"pt-br"},"637":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"**Abra uma pasta** (Arquivo > Abrir Pasta). Se ela ainda não tem um\nworkspace Brokspace, a visão Brokspace oferece **Configurar Workspace**:\nela roda `brok init` para você.","locale":"pt-br"},"638":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"**Pergunte.** Digite uma pergunta na página inicial ou no painel do\nagente: o agente Brokspace responde com o seu LLM e cita as fontes usadas;\nclique em uma fonte para abrir o arquivo naquela linha. Perguntas de\nacompanhamento mantêm a conversa. Pressione `Ctrl+Shift+A`\n(`Cmd+Shift+A` no macOS) para o **modo foco no agente**, em que o agente\nocupa a maior parte da janela.","locale":"pt-br"},"639":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"**Busque.** A visão Brokspace (o \"B\" dobrado na barra de atividades)\nencontra código pelo significado ou pelo nome; clique em um resultado para\nabri-lo.","locale":"pt-br"},"640":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#seus-primeiros-minutos","content":"**Revise e faça commit.** Digite `/review` no chat (ou `/review staged`,\n`/review base main`). No Controle de Código-Fonte, o botão ✨ escreve a\nmensagem de commit a partir das alterações preparadas.","locale":"pt-br"},"641":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#a-visão-brokspace","content":"| Seção           | O que mostra                                                                            |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Visão Geral** | Se o Brokspace está rodando, o modelo, o índice, a busca e Perguntar / Revisar / Commit |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"642":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-18","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#a-visão-brokspace","content":"| Seção      | O que mostra                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Shards** | Cada shard instalado e seu estado; expanda um para ver o que ele lê e escreve, se usa a rede, os programas que executa, os eventos que escuta e publica, e de onde veio. Instale, crie ou remova shards pela barra de ferramentas |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"643":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-19","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#a-visão-brokspace","content":"| Seção      | O que mostra                                                                                |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Skills** | Fluxos de trabalho que você executa e as skills que seus agentes usam; clique para executar |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"644":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-20","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"Toda solicitação passa pelo `brok`, que a envia ao LLM definido em\n`.brokspace/brok.yml` (Ollama, LM Studio ou uma API hospedada compatível com\nOpenAI). Sem um LLM, ou quando ele não responde, o agente responde com o que\no índice local encontrou, em forma de links.","locale":"pt-br"},"645":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-21","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"| Digite       | Ele executa                        |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| Uma pergunta | `brok ask` com a conversa até aqui |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"646":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-22","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"| Digite    | Ele executa                                    |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `/review` | Uma revisão das suas alterações não commitadas |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"647":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-23","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"| Digite           | Ele executa                           |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `/review staged` | Uma revisão das alterações preparadas |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"648":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"| Digite               | Ele executa                                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `/review base <ref>` | Uma revisão deste branch em relação a `<ref>` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"649":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-25","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#o-agente-brokspace","content":"| Digite                    | Ele executa                                                                     |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/skill <nome> <entrada>` | Uma skill no seu LLM, por exemplo `/skill tdd adicionar um campo de prioridade` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"650":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-26","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#comandos-e-idiomas","content":"Tudo também está no menu **Brokspace** e na paleta de comandos: Configurar\nWorkspace, Iniciar / Parar / Reiniciar, Reconstruir Índice, Diagnóstico,\nInstalar, Criar e Remover Shard, Exportar Skills para Agentes de Código,\nExecutar Skill, Revisar, Escrever Mensagem de Commit. A barra de status\nmostra se o Brokspace está rodando e qual modelo ele usa.","locale":"pt-br"},"651":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-27","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#comandos-e-idiomas","content":"A IDE está em inglês e em português do Brasil. Ela começa em português em um\nsistema em português; troque em **Idioma** na página inicial.","locale":"pt-br"},"652":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/ide-28","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/ide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/ide#como-funciona","content":"A IDE conversa com o Brokspace apenas pela CLI `brok` e sua saída JSON (veja\nIntegrações), então ela mostra exatamente o que o\n`brok` vê, e tudo o que ela faz você também pode fazer em um terminal. Ela\nprecisa do brok 0.2.4 ou mais recente; o que vem com ela atende.","locale":"pt-br"},"653":{"id":"/pt-br/docs","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","type":"page","content":"Introdução","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Início"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs","locale":"pt-br"},"654":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs","content":"O Brokspace deixa qualquer workspace de desenvolvimento pesquisável e pronto para agentes, na sua máquina.","locale":"pt-br"},"655":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs#duas-formas-de-usar","content":"Duas formas de usar","locale":"pt-br"},"656":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"O que você ganha","locale":"pt-br"},"657":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"Comece","locale":"pt-br"},"658":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs","content":"O Brokspace (`brok`) indexa seu código (um repositório, seus submódulos ou\numa pasta inteira de repositórios) em um mecanismo de busca híbrido local,\nconecta esse índice ao LLM que você escolher e o liga aos agentes de código\nque você já usa. Nada sai da sua máquina, a menos que você escolha um modelo\nhospedado.","locale":"pt-br"},"659":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#duas-formas-de-usar","content":"Em qualquer terminal e qualquer editor. `brok search`, `ask`, `chat`,\n`review`, `commit`, skills e shards. Seus agentes de código ganham a\nferramenta `brok_search` via MCP.","locale":"pt-br"},"660":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#duas-formas-de-usar","content":"O mesmo workspace em uma IDE feita em torno dele: uma página inicial que\ncomeça pela sua pergunta, o agente Brokspace no chat, busca, revisões e\nmensagens de commit a um clique.","locale":"pt-br"},"661":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#duas-formas-de-usar","content":"Os dois compartilham a mesma pasta `.brokspace/`, então você pode alternar a\nqualquer momento.","locale":"pt-br"},"662":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"**Busca que entende código.** Funções, classes e seções são indexadas\ninteiras e encontradas pelo significado ou pelo nome, em todos os\nrepositórios.","locale":"pt-br"},"663":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"**Respostas com fontes.** Pergunte ao seu próprio LLM (Ollama, LM Studio ou\num modelo hospedado) sobre o workspace; toda resposta lista o código usado.","locale":"pt-br"},"664":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"**Revisões e mensagens de commit** a partir das suas alterações preparadas\nou não commitadas.","locale":"pt-br"},"665":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"**Skills:** 20 fluxos de trabalho para IA já incluídos (TDD, code review,\nespecificações...) e os seus próprios em um `SKILL.md`.","locale":"pt-br"},"666":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#o-que-você-ganha","content":"**Shards:** pequenos programas que reagem ao seu workspace por meio de um\nbarramento de eventos local e com permissões.","locale":"pt-br"},"667":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"Instale, configure seu primeiro workspace e use no dia a dia: cerca de 15\nminutos.","locale":"pt-br"},"668":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"Escolha um modelo adequado à sua máquina e rode com Ollama ou LM Studio.","locale":"pt-br"},"669":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"Os fluxos de trabalho incluídos e como escrever e compartilhar os seus.","locale":"pt-br"},"670":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"Crie integrações que reagem ao seu workspace.","locale":"pt-br"},"671":{"id":"/pt-br/docs-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs#comece","content":"O Brokspace é código aberto (MIT ou Apache-2.0). Perguntas e ideias vão para\nas GitHub Discussions.","locale":"pt-br"},"672":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","type":"page","content":"Integrations","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Guias"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","locale":"pt-br"},"673":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"Coding agents","locale":"pt-br"},"674":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#local-and-hosted-llms","content":"Local and hosted LLMs","locale":"pt-br"},"675":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"Editors and scripts: JSON output","locale":"pt-br"},"676":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#shards-integrations-you-build","content":"Shards: integrations you build","locale":"pt-br"},"677":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"Brokspace stays small and plugs into the tools you already use.","locale":"pt-br"},"678":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration                                                   | How                | Setup               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code / Copilot, Codex) | MCP tools + skills | `brok setup agents` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"679":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration                    | How                   | Setup            |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Local LLMs (Ollama, LM Studio) | OpenAI-compatible API | `brok setup llm` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"680":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration                                              | How                           | Setup              |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Hosted LLMs (Anthropic, DeepSeek, any OpenAI-compatible) | `llm.providers` in `brok.yml` | export the API key |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"681":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration        | How                                  | Setup     |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | --------- |\n| Git and submodules | change tracking, hot/cold partitions | automatic |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"682":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration                           | How             | Setup             |\n| ------------------------------------- | --------------- | ----------------- |\n| Team storage (S3, R2, MinIO, Git LFS) | index mirroring | `brok setup sync` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"683":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","content":"| Integration   | How           | Setup            |\n| ------------- | ------------- | ---------------- |\n| Anything else | write a shard | `brok shard new` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"684":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"For each agent it does two things.","locale":"pt-br"},"685":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"**1. MCP server.** Registers `brok mcp` (a stdio\nModel Context Protocol server) so the\nagent gets two tools:","locale":"pt-br"},"686":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Tool          | What it does                                                                              |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok_search` | Hybrid search over the local index; returns whole functions/classes with `path:start-end` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"687":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Tool          | What it does                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `brok_status` | What is indexed and whether `brok run` is active |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"688":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Agent       | File written                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json` (`mcpServers.brokspace`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"689":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Agent  | File written                                |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Cursor | `.cursor/mcp.json` (`mcpServers.brokspace`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"690":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Agent             | File written                             |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| VS Code / Copilot | `.vscode/mcp.json` (`servers.brokspace`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"691":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-18","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"| Agent | File written                                  |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Codex | prints the snippet for `~/.codex/config.toml` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-2"},"692":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-19","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"Existing entries in those files are preserved; only `brokspace` is added or\nupdated. When `brok run` is active, searches reuse its loaded model;\notherwise `brok mcp` opens the index read-only on demand.","locale":"pt-br"},"693":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-20","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"**2. Skills.** Exports the skills to `.claude/skills/` (Claude\nCode) and `.agents/skills/` (Codex, Cursor, Copilot and others), so `/ask-brok`,\n`/grill-me`, `tdd`, `code-review` and the rest are available in the agent.","locale":"pt-br"},"694":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-21","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#coding-agents","content":"Commit the generated files to give your whole team the same setup. `brok`\nmust be on `PATH` for agents to start `brok mcp`; `brok doctor` checks it.","locale":"pt-br"},"695":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-22","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#local-and-hosted-llms","content":"See Local LLM setup. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works:","locale":"pt-br"},"696":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-23","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"Editors (the Brokspace IDE among them), scripts and CI read brok through\n`--json`. Shapes are stable within a minor version.","locale":"pt-br"},"697":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"| Command              | Output                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok status --json` | One document: `version`, `initialized`, `root`, `daemon.running`, `backends`, `embeddings`, `llm` (`provider`, `model`, `base_url`), `index[]` (`tier`, `path`, `files`, `chunks`, `backend`, `semantic`), `shards[]` (`name`, `version`, `description`, `state`, `source`). Outside a workspace: `{\"version\": ..., \"initialized\": false}`. |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"698":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-25","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"| Command                      | Output                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok search <query> --json` | One document: `hits[]` with `path`, `start_line`, `end_line`, `kind`, `symbol`, `score`, `content`. |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"699":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-26","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"| Command                  | Output                                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok skill list --json` | One array: `name`, `description`, `user_invoked`, `source`, `bucket` per skill. |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"700":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-27","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"| Command                                                                  | Output                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok ask ... --json`, `brok review --json`, `brok skill run ... --json` | A stream, one JSON event per line (see below). |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-3"},"701":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-28","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"Streaming events:","locale":"pt-br"},"702":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-29","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#editors-and-scripts-json-output","content":"A failure ends the stream with a non-zero exit code and the message on\nstderr. Follow-up questions pass the conversation so far:\n`brok ask --json --history turns.json \"and where is it tested?\"`, where\n`turns.json` holds `[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...\"}, {\"role\":\n\"assistant\", \"content\": \"...\"}]`.","locale":"pt-br"},"703":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations-30","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/integrations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/integrations#shards-integrations-you-build","content":"When something is specific to your team (a ticketing system, a deploy\npipeline, a compliance check), write a shard instead of waiting for a core\nfeature: it reacts to workspace events and publishes its own. See\nShards and start with `brok shard new my-integration`.","locale":"pt-br"},"704":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"page","content":"Local LLM setup","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Guias"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","locale":"pt-br"},"705":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","content":"Brokspace answers questions (brok ask) and runs skills (brok skill run) with any OpenAI-compatible model.","locale":"pt-br"},"706":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"The short version","locale":"pt-br"},"707":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"What your machine can run","locale":"pt-br"},"708":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-1-ollama-recommended-terminal-friendly","content":"Option 1: Ollama (recommended, terminal friendly)","locale":"pt-br"},"709":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-2-lm-studio-graphical","content":"Option 2: LM Studio (graphical)","locale":"pt-br"},"710":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#hosted-models","content":"Hosted models","locale":"pt-br"},"711":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#using-the-same-model-elsewhere","content":"Using the same model elsewhere","locale":"pt-br"},"712":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#performance-tips","content":"Performance tips","locale":"pt-br"},"713":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","content":"Brokspace answers questions (`brok ask`) and runs skills (`brok skill run`)\nwith any OpenAI-compatible model. Running it locally keeps everything\n**free, private and offline**. Search and indexing never need an LLM.","locale":"pt-br"},"714":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"It:","locale":"pt-br"},"715":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"reads your RAM (and NVIDIA GPU memory) and picks a model size from the\ntable below;","locale":"pt-br"},"716":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"looks for a running **Ollama** (`localhost:11434`) or **LM Studio**\n(`localhost:1234`) server;","locale":"pt-br"},"717":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"uses a model you already have, or offers to download the recommended one\n(`ollama pull`);","locale":"pt-br"},"718":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"writes the choice to `.brokspace/brok.yml` (`llm.default`).","locale":"pt-br"},"719":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#the-short-version","content":"Nothing installed yet? It prints the one-line install for your OS. Run it,\nthen `brok setup llm` again. `brok doctor` tells you at any time whether the\nmodel is reachable.","locale":"pt-br"},"720":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"Sizes are for 4-bit quantized models (`Q4_K_M`), the best balance between\nspeed and quality.","locale":"pt-br"},"721":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"| Model size | Memory and GPU | Typical hardware                 | Recommended (Ollama)                |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| 1B to 3B   | 8 GB           | Office laptops, entry-level Macs | `qwen2.5-coder:1.5b`, `llama3.2:3b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"722":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"| Model size | Memory and GPU | Typical hardware                          | Recommended (Ollama)              |\n| ---------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| 3B         | 16 GB, no GPU  | Business laptops with integrated graphics | `qwen2.5-coder:3b`, `llama3.2:3b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"723":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-18","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"| Model size                | Memory and GPU                                                 | Typical hardware                        | Recommended (Ollama)                              |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **7B to 9B** (sweet spot) | 16 GB with a GPU (6 GB+) or Apple Silicon; 32 GB without a GPU | Gaming laptops, M1/M2/M3 Macs, desktops | `qwen2.5-coder:7b`, `llama3:8b`, `deepseek-r1:8b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"724":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-19","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"| Model size | Memory and GPU                                          | Typical hardware                      | Recommended (Ollama)                   |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| 14B to 32B | A GPU with 12 GB+, or 32 GB with a GPU or Apple Silicon | Workstations, Mac Pro/Max with 32 GB+ | `qwen2.5-coder:14b`, `deepseek-r1:32b` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"725":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-20","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"Without a GPU the model runs on the processor: memory decides what fits,\nbut speed decides what is pleasant. A laptop CPU reads a long prompt into a\n7B model at about 15 tokens per second, so a review takes 3 to 5 minutes;\na 3B model is about twice as fast. That is why machines without a GPU get\none size smaller. Only NVIDIA GPUs and Apple Silicon are detected; with\nanother GPU that Ollama supports, pick the row for your GPU memory.","locale":"pt-br"},"726":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-21","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"What to expect: 1B to 3B models answer questions about your code well\nenough (`brok ask`, `brok chat`), but they lose track of longer skills, so\n`brok review`, `brok commit` and most `brok skill run` workflows are much\nbetter with 7B or larger. Even at 7B, a review is a first pass that can be\nwrong; 14B and hosted models (`brok review -p anthropic`) review much\nbetter, and commit messages are already good at 7B.","locale":"pt-br"},"727":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-22","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#what-your-machine-can-run","content":"`brok setup llm` applies exactly this table. Override it any time:","locale":"pt-br"},"728":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-23","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-1-ollama-recommended-terminal-friendly","content":"| OS      | Install                                                         |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Windows | `winget install Ollama.Ollama` or the installer from ollama.com |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"729":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-1-ollama-recommended-terminal-friendly","content":"| OS    | Install                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| macOS | `brew install ollama` or the app from ollama.com |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"730":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-25","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-1-ollama-recommended-terminal-friendly","content":"| OS    | Install                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Linux | `curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh \\| sh` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"731":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-26","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-2-lm-studio-graphical","content":"Download it from lmstudio.ai (Windows `.exe`,\nmacOS `.dmg` for Apple Silicon or Intel, Linux `.AppImage`:\n`chmod +x LM_Studio-*.AppImage && ./LM_Studio-*.AppImage`).","locale":"pt-br"},"732":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-27","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-2-lm-studio-graphical","content":"Search for `Qwen2.5-Coder-7B` (or the size from the table), pick a\n`Q4_K_M` or `Q5_K_M` file and download it.","locale":"pt-br"},"733":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-28","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-2-lm-studio-graphical","content":"Open the **Developer / Local Server** tab, load the model and press\n**Start Server** (it listens on `http://localhost:1234`).","locale":"pt-br"},"734":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-29","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#option-2-lm-studio-graphical","content":"Run `brok setup llm`: it finds the server and lets you pick the model.","locale":"pt-br"},"735":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-30","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#hosted-models","content":"Prefer a hosted model for some questions? Export its key and choose it per\nrequest; the providers are preconfigured in `brok.yml`:","locale":"pt-br"},"736":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-31","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#hosted-models","content":"Keys are read from the environment, never stored in `brok.yml`, and secrets\nfound in retrieved code are redacted before any prompt leaves your machine.","locale":"pt-br"},"737":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-32","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#using-the-same-model-elsewhere","content":"**Aider**: `aider --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b` inside your git\nrepository (`pip install aider-chat`, Python 3.10 to 3.12).","locale":"pt-br"},"738":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-33","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#using-the-same-model-elsewhere","content":"**Coding agents** (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Codex): `brok setup agents`\ngives them the Brokspace search tool and skills; see\nIntegrations.","locale":"pt-br"},"739":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-34","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#performance-tips","content":"**Apple Silicon**: memory is unified, so a 16 GB Mac runs 7B/8B models fast.","locale":"pt-br"},"740":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-35","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#performance-tips","content":"**NVIDIA / AMD GPUs**: enable full GPU offload in LM Studio or Ollama.","locale":"pt-br"},"741":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-36","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#performance-tips","content":"**Storage**: keep models on an SSD; loading from a spinning disk is painfully slow.","locale":"pt-br"},"742":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm-37","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/local-llm#performance-tips","content":"**Smaller is often better** for interactive use: a fast 7B beats a slow\n14B for everyday questions; switch per request with `-p`.","locale":"pt-br"},"743":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"page","content":"Shards","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Guias"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards","locale":"pt-br"},"744":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards","content":"Shards are small programs that react to workspace events.","locale":"pt-br"},"745":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"Lifecycle","locale":"pt-br"},"746":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"`shard.json`","locale":"pt-br"},"747":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#topics","content":"Topics","locale":"pt-br"},"748":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"Runtime contract","locale":"pt-br"},"749":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"Using the SDK","locale":"pt-br"},"750":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#security","content":"Security","locale":"pt-br"},"751":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards","content":"Shards are small programs that react to workspace events. Each one is a\nseparate process connected to the `brok run` event bus, restricted to the\ntopics its manifest declares.","locale":"pt-br"},"752":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards","content":"The fastest way to write one is the\nbrok-shard-template\nrepository; this page is the reference.","locale":"pt-br"},"753":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"To trigger your shard by hand, publish the event it listens to:\n`brok bus emit file:changed '{\"changed\":[\"src/main.rs\"],\"deleted\":[]}'`.\nWindows PowerShell 5.1 drops the inner double quotes when it calls a\nprogram, so escape them there: `'{\\\"changed\\\":[\\\"src/main.rs\\\"],\\\"deleted\\\":[]}'`\n(PowerShell 7 and other shells need no escaping).","locale":"pt-br"},"754":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"Installing:","locale":"pt-br"},"755":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"clones the repository (`--depth 1`, optional `--tag`) or uses the local directory;","locale":"pt-br"},"756":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"validates `shard.json` and the `brok` version requirement;","locale":"pt-br"},"757":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"**shows the requested capabilities and asks for consent** (`--yes` to skip in scripts);","locale":"pt-br"},"758":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"obtains the executable, in order of preference:","locale":"pt-br"},"759":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"a release asset for this platform, verified against its SHA-256;","locale":"pt-br"},"760":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"the manifest's `build.command`, run in the repository;","locale":"pt-br"},"761":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"an `entrypoint` already present in the repository;","locale":"pt-br"},"762":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-18","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"moves it into `.brokspace/shards/<name>/` and records the source, commit and\nbinary hash in `shards.lock`.","locale":"pt-br"},"763":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-19","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#lifecycle","content":"Disable a shard without removing it in `brok.yml`:","locale":"pt-br"},"764":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-20","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field  | Required | Rules                                             |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `name` | ✓        | `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$`, unique in the workspace |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"765":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-21","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field     | Required | Rules  |\n| --------- | -------- | ------ |\n| `version` | ✓        | SemVer |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"766":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-22","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field        | Required | Rules                                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entrypoint` | ✓¹       | Relative path inside the shard directory; `.exe` is appended on Windows |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"767":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-23","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field    | Required | Rules                                                        |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `skills` | ✓¹       | Directories whose subfolders each hold a `SKILL.md` (skills) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"768":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field  | Required | Rules                                     |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `brok` |          | SemVer requirement on the runtime version |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"769":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-25","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field     | Required | Rules              |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `runtime` |          | `native` (default) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"770":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-26","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field                               | Required | Rules                                                |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.filesystem.read/write` |          | Workspace relative paths, no `..`, no absolute paths |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"771":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-27","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field                 | Required | Rules              |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `permissions.network` |          | `false` by default |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"772":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-28","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field                 | Required | Rules                                       |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.process` |          | Bare program names the shard intends to run |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"773":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-29","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field             | Required | Rules                                                                                  |\n| ----------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.env` |          | Variables to pass through: exact names, `PREFIX_*` or `*_SUFFIX`. `BROK_*` is reserved |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"774":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-30","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field                            | Required | Rules                                                            |\n| -------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subscribes_to` / `publishes_to` |          | Topic patterns; publishing to `system:*` (or `*`) is not allowed |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"775":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-31","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field           | Required | Rules                                             |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build.command` |          | Program + arguments, executed **without a shell** |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"776":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-32","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"| Field                  | Required | Rules                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `releases.<os>-<arch>` |          | `https://` URL and 64 hex SHA-256; keys use Rust's `std::env::consts` names (`linux-x86_64`, `macos-aarch64`, `windows-x86_64`, …) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"777":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-33","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"¹ A shard needs an `entrypoint`, `skills`, or both. Skill-only shards run no\nprocess, so they cannot declare topics, `build` or `releases`.","locale":"pt-br"},"778":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-34","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#shardjson","content":"Unknown fields are rejected, and all violations are reported at once.","locale":"pt-br"},"779":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-35","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#topics","content":"`namespace:name`, lowercase letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.` for sub-topics:\n`file:changed`, `agent:ask.chunk`. Patterns are exact topics or a prefix\nending in `*` (`agent:ask.*`, `file:*`, `*`). Pick a namespace named after\nyour shard for your own events. The well-known topics and their payloads are\nlisted in Architecture.","locale":"pt-br"},"780":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-36","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"`brok run` starts the entrypoint with:","locale":"pt-br"},"781":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-37","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"working directory = workspace root;","locale":"pt-br"},"782":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-38","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"an environment containing only OS basics (`PATH`, `HOME`, `TEMP`, …),\n`RUST_LOG`, the variables allowed by `permissions.env`, and:","locale":"pt-br"},"783":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-39","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable        | Value                              |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_ENDPOINT` | Socket path / pipe name of the bus |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"784":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-40","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable     | Value                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_TOKEN` | The shard's session token (secret) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"785":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-41","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable          | Value         |\n| ----------------- | ------------- |\n| `BROK_SHARD_NAME` | Manifest name |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"786":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-42","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable         | Value                   |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `BROK_WORKSPACE` | Absolute workspace root |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"787":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-43","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable                         | Value                         |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `BROK_FS_READ` / `BROK_FS_WRITE` | Declared paths, `;`-separated |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"788":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-44","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"| Variable       | Value      |\n| -------------- | ---------- |\n| `BROK_NETWORK` | `1` or `0` |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-1"},"789":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-45","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"stdout and stderr are captured line by line, prefixed with the shard name in\nthe `brok run` output and appended to `.brokspace/logs/<name>.log`. Log to\nstderr.","locale":"pt-br"},"790":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-46","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"On `system:shutdown` (delivered without subscribing), exit within 3 seconds.","locale":"pt-br"},"791":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-47","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#runtime-contract","content":"A non-zero exit is a crash: the shard is restarted with backoff.","locale":"pt-br"},"792":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-48","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"Typed payloads implement `brok_sdk::Payload` (a serde type plus its topic).","locale":"pt-br"},"793":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-49","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"`client.request(event)` returns a stream of replies; `client.call::<Req,\nRes>(&req, timeout)` waits for the first typed reply. Example: query the\nindex with `client.call::<SearchRequest, SearchResults>(…)` (add\n`index:search` to `publishes_to`).","locale":"pt-br"},"794":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-50","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"`client.reply(&request, &payload)` answers a request; only the requester\nreceives it.","locale":"pt-br"},"795":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-51","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"`client.context()` returns the workspace root, your `shards.<name>.settings`\nfrom `brok.yml` and the `llm` routing table.","locale":"pt-br"},"796":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-52","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#using-the-sdk","content":"Shards do not have to be written in Rust: anything that can open a Unix\nsocket / named pipe and exchange length-prefixed JSON frames works. The frame\nformat is documented in `brok-sdk/src/frame.rs` and `codec.rs`.","locale":"pt-br"},"797":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-53","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#security","content":"What the runtime **enforces**: topic ACLs, `source` stamping, reply routing,\nthe scrubbed environment, the working directory.","locale":"pt-br"},"798":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/shards-54","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/shards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/shards#security","content":"What is **declared but not yet enforced by the OS**: file system and network\naccess. Consent at install time is the safeguard until OS sandboxes (Landlock,\nSeatbelt, AppContainer) land. `build.command` runs arbitrary code from the\nshard repository (e.g. `build.rs`) — the consent prompt shows it before it\nruns. Prefer shards that publish checksum-pinned `releases`.","locale":"pt-br"},"799":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"page","content":"Skills","breadcrumbs":["Brokspace","Guias"],"tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills","locale":"pt-br"},"800":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-0","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills","content":"A skill is a small, reusable workflow written for AI agents: a folder with a SKILL.md (YAML frontmatter name + description, then instructions) and optional reference files.","locale":"pt-br"},"801":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-1","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#two-kinds","content":"Two kinds","locale":"pt-br"},"802":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-2","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#built-in-skills","content":"Built-in skills","locale":"pt-br"},"803":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-3","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#using-skills","content":"Using skills","locale":"pt-br"},"804":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-4","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#writing-your-own","content":"Writing your own","locale":"pt-br"},"805":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-5","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#sharing-skills-skill-shards","content":"Sharing skills: skill shards","locale":"pt-br"},"806":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-6","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#precedence","content":"Precedence","locale":"pt-br"},"807":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-7","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#credits","content":"Credits","locale":"pt-br"},"808":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-8","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills","content":"A **skill** is a small, reusable workflow written for AI agents: a folder\nwith a `SKILL.md` (YAML frontmatter `name` + `description`, then\ninstructions) and optional reference files. Brokspace uses the same\nAgent Skills format as Claude Code,\nCodex, Cursor and GitHub Copilot, so a skill written once works everywhere.","locale":"pt-br"},"809":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-9","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#two-kinds","content":"|               | User-invoked                | Model-invoked                        |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Who starts it | Only you, by typing `/name` | You, or the agent when the task fits |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"810":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-10","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#two-kinds","content":"|             | User-invoked                     | Model-invoked |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| Frontmatter | `disable-model-invocation: true` | (default)     |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"811":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-11","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#two-kinds","content":"|      | User-invoked                                | Model-invoked                                |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Role | Orchestrates a flow (`/to-spec`, `/triage`) | A reusable discipline (`tdd`, `code-review`) |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"812":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-12","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#two-kinds","content":"|             | User-invoked          | Model-invoked               |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Description | One human-facing line | Rich \"Use when...\" triggers |","locale":"pt-br","table":"table-0"},"813":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-13","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#built-in-skills","content":"`brok` ships a curated set, embedded in the binary (source:\nskills/). They cover the whole development loop that\nBrokspace itself uses: align, specify, slice, build test-first, review, ship.","locale":"pt-br"},"814":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-14","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#built-in-skills","content":"Not sure where to start? Type `/ask-brok` in your coding agent and describe\nyour situation.","locale":"pt-br"},"815":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-15","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#using-skills","content":"**In your coding agent** (the main way):","locale":"pt-br"},"816":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-16","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#using-skills","content":"Skills land in `.claude/skills/` and the portable `.agents/skills/` (read by\nCodex, Cursor, Copilot and others). Folders are marked `.brokspace-managed`\nand refreshed on every export; brok never overwrites a folder it did not\ncreate. Commit them to share with your team.","locale":"pt-br"},"817":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-17","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#using-skills","content":"**On your local LLM**, through `brok-agent` (needs `brok run`):","locale":"pt-br"},"818":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-18","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#using-skills","content":"The skill's instructions (and the reference files it links) become the\nsystem prompt; Brokspace adds relevant code from the index as context.","locale":"pt-br"},"819":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-19","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#writing-your-own","content":"Workspace skills in `.brokspace/skills/<name>/` **override** built-ins with\nthe same name, so you can tailor any built-in to your team. Keep skills\nshort and explicit: small local models follow them too. The built-in\n`write-skill` skill walks your agent through it.","locale":"pt-br"},"820":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-20","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#sharing-skills-skill-shards","content":"A **skill shard** is a shard with no process, just skills. Publish it as a\ngit repository and anyone can install it:","locale":"pt-br"},"821":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-21","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#sharing-skills-skill-shards","content":"`shard.json` of a skill shard:","locale":"pt-br"},"822":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-22","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#sharing-skills-skill-shards","content":"A shard can also ship skills next to its process (`entrypoint` + `skills`).","locale":"pt-br"},"823":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-23","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#precedence","content":"When names collide, the first wins: workspace (`.brokspace/skills/`) >\ninstalled shards > built-in. `brok skill list` reports shadowed skills.","locale":"pt-br"},"824":{"id":"/pt-br/docs/skills-24","page_id":"/pt-br/docs/skills","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/pt-br/docs/skills#credits","content":"The built-in workflows are adapted from\nmattpocock/skills (MIT); see\nskills/CREDITS.md.","locale":"pt-br"}},"count":824},"sorting":{"language":"multilingual","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"so