0":419,"821":123,"822":435,"823":802,"824":721},"orderedDocs":[[273,"**1. MCP server.** Registers `brok mcp` (a stdio\nModel Context Protocol server) so the\nagent gets two tools:"],[685,"**1. MCP server.** Registers `brok mcp` (a stdio\nModel Context Protocol server) so the\nagent gets two tools:"],[281,"**2. Skills.** Exports the skills to `.claude/skills/` (Claude\nCode) and `.agents/skills/` (Codex, Cursor, Copilot and others), so `/ask-brok`,\n`/grill-me`, `tdd`, `code-review` and the rest are available in the agent."],[693,"**2. Skills.** Exports the skills to `.claude/skills/` (Claude\nCode) and `.agents/skills/` (Codex, Cursor, Copilot and others), so `/ask-brok`,\n`/grill-me`, `tdd`, `code-review` and the rest are available in the agent."],[160,"**About AI reviews.** With a local 7b model, `brok review` is a quick first\npass: it catches slips you would rather not push, but it also gets things\nwrong (we have seen it invent a missing validation). Read its findings as\nquestions, not verdicts. For a review you want to rely on, use a 14b model\nor a hosted one for that run: `brok review -p anthropic` (see\nConfigure for API keys)."],[572,"**About AI reviews.** With a local 7b model, `brok review` is a quick first\npass: it catches slips you would rather not push, but it also gets things\nwrong (we have seen it invent a missing validation). Read its findings as\nquestions, not verdicts. For a review you want to rely on, use a 14b model\nor a hosted one for that run: `brok review -p anthropic` (see\nConfigure for API keys)."],[637,"**Abra uma pasta** (Arquivo > Abrir Pasta). Se ela ainda não tem um\nworkspace Brokspace, a visão Brokspace oferece **Configurar Workspace**:\nela roda `brok init` para você."],[325,"**Aider**: `aider --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b` inside your git\nrepository (`pip install aider-chat`, Python 3.10 to 3.12)."],[737,"**Aider**: `aider --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b` inside your git\nrepository (`pip install aider-chat`, Python 3.10 to 3.12)."],[251,"**Answers with sources.** Ask your own LLM (Ollama, LM Studio, or a hosted\nmodel) about the workspace; every answer lists the code it used."],[177,"**API keys** are never written to files: export them in your shell\n(`export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`, or `$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"...\"` in\nPowerShell) and Brokspace reads them when needed. Secrets found in your code\nare removed from the context before anything is sent to an LLM."],[589,"**API keys** are never written to files: export them in your shell\n(`export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`, or `$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"...\"` in\nPowerShell) and Brokspace reads them when needed. Secrets found in your code\nare removed from the context before anything is sent to an LLM."],[327,"**Apple Silicon**: memory is unified, so a 16 GB Mac runs 7B/8B models fast."],[739,"**Apple Silicon**: memory is unified, so a 16 GB Mac runs 7B/8B models fast."],[24,"**Arrow IPC**: each commit writes a new immutable generation file and flips\n`CURRENT`. Files are memory-mapped and decoded zero-copy; immutability is\nwhat makes `mmap` sound and lets readers keep an old generation (Windows\ncannot replace a mapped file). Vector search is exact (dot product over\nnormalized vectors)."],[436,"**Arrow IPC**: each commit writes a new immutable generation file and flips\n`CURRENT`. Files are memory-mapped and decoded zero-copy; immutability is\nwhat makes `mmap` sound and lets readers keep an old generation (Windows\ncannot replace a mapped file). Vector search is exact (dot product over\nnormalized vectors)."],[226,"**Ask.** Type a question on the home page or in the agent panel: the\nBrokspace agent answers from your LLM with the sources it used; click a\nsource to open the file at that line. Follow-up questions keep the\nconversation. Press `Ctrl+Shift+A` (`Cmd+Shift+A` on macOS) for **agent\nfocus mode**, where the agent takes most of the window."],[662,"**Busca que entende código.** Funções, classes e seções são indexadas\ninteiras e encontradas pelo significado ou pelo nome, em todos os\nrepositórios."],[639,"**Busque.** A visão Brokspace (o \"B\" dobrado na barra de atividades)\nencontra código pelo significado ou pelo nome; clique em um resultado para\nabri-lo."],[18,"**Chunk** in parallel (rayon). The AST chunker emits one chunk per\ndefinition, attaches doc comments/attributes/decorators, splits large\ncontainers into a header plus members (`parent` = the container) and\ngroups loose top-level code into `preamble` chunks."],[430,"**Chunk** in parallel (rayon). The AST chunker emits one chunk per\ndefinition, attaches doc comments/attributes/decorators, splits large\ncontainers into a header plus members (`parent` = the container) and\ngroups loose top-level code into `preamble` chunks."],[326,"**Coding agents** (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Codex): `brok setup agents`\ngives them the Brokspace search tool and skills; see\nIntegrations."],[738,"**Coding agents** (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Codex): `brok setup agents`\ngives them the Brokspace search tool and skills; see\nIntegrations."],[123,"**Company laptop blocks the script?** Download `brok-windows-x86_64.exe`\nfrom the brok release\nand `brok-agent-windows-x86_64.exe` from the\nagent release,\nrename them `brok.exe` and `brok-agent.exe`, put both in one folder and add\nthat folder to your `PATH`."],[535,"**Company laptop blocks the script?** Download `brok-windows-x86_64.exe`\nfrom the brok release\nand `brok-agent-windows-x86_64.exe` from the\nagent release,\nrename them `brok.exe` and `brok-agent.exe`, put both in one folder and add\nthat folder to your `PATH`."],[19,"**Embed** in batches on a blocking thread (`spawn_blocking`), prefixing\n`search_document:` as nomic models expect; mean pooling → layer norm →\nMatryoshka truncation → L2 normalization."],[431,"**Embed** in batches on a blocking thread (`spawn_blocking`), prefixing\n`search_document:` as nomic models expect; mean pooling → layer norm →\nMatryoshka truncation → L2 normalization."],[27,"**Handshake**: `Hello{protocol, name, version, token}` → `Welcome{session,\nidentity, context}` or `Error`. Tokens are 256-bit random, stored hashed."],[439,"**Handshake**: `Hello{protocol, name, version, token}` → `Welcome{session,\nidentity, context}` or `Error`. Tokens are 256-bit random, stored hashed."],[403,"**In your coding agent** (the main way):"],[815,"**In your coding agent** (the main way):"],[620,"**Instalação com um comando** pela CLI e pela Brokspace IDE."],[23,"**LanceDB**: deletes/appends go straight to the table; compaction runs every\n16 writes and an ANN index is built past 10 000 rows."],[435,"**LanceDB**: deletes/appends go straight to the table; compaction runs every\n16 writes and an ANN index is built past 10 000 rows."],[120,"**macOS / Linux**"],[532,"**macOS / Linux**"],[328,"**NVIDIA / AMD GPUs**: enable full GPU offload in LM Studio or Ollama."],[740,"**NVIDIA / AMD GPUs**: enable full GPU offload in LM Studio or Ollama."],[207,"**Official shards and skill packs**, reviewed and versioned."],[126,"**Ollama** (recommended):"],[538,"**Ollama** (recommended):"],[405,"**On your local LLM**, through `brok-agent` (needs `brok run`):"],[817,"**On your local LLM**, through `brok-agent` (needs `brok run`):"],[208,"**One-command install** from the CLI and from the Brokspace IDE."],[225,"**Open a folder** (File > Open Folder). If it has no Brokspace workspace\nyet, the Brokspace view offers **Set Up Workspace**: it runs `brok init`\nfor you."],[638,"**Pergunte.** Digite uma pergunta na página inicial ou no painel do\nagente: o agente Brokspace responde com o seu LLM e cita as fontes usadas;\nclique em uma fonte para abrir o arquivo naquela linha. Perguntas de\nacompanhamento mantêm a conversa. Pressione `Ctrl+Shift+A`\n(`Cmd+Shift+A` no macOS) para o **modo foco no agente**, em que o agente\nocupa a maior parte da janela."],[209,"**Permissions up front:** every shard lists what it may read, write, run\nand reach, before you install it."],[621,"**Permissões às claras:** cada shard lista o que pode ler, escrever,\nexecutar e acessar antes de você instalá-lo."],[124,"**Prefer Cargo?** `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent` (needs a C compiler and\n`protoc`), or `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent --no-default-features` for a\nlighter build with text search only."],[536,"**Prefer Cargo?** `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent` (needs a C compiler and\n`protoc`), or `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent --no-default-features` for a\nlighter build with text search only."],[663,"**Respostas com fontes.** Pergunte ao seu próprio LLM (Ollama, LM Studio ou\num modelo hospedado) sobre o workspace; toda resposta lista o código usado."],[228,"**Review and commit.** Type `/review` in the chat (or `/review staged`,\n`/review base main`). In Source Control, the ✨ button writes the commit\nmessage from the staged changes."],[252,"**Reviews and commit messages** from your staged or uncommitted changes."],[640,"**Revise e faça commit.** Digite `/review` no chat (ou `/review staged`,\n`/review base main`). No Controle de Código-Fonte, o botão ✨ escreve a\nmensagem de commit a partir das alterações preparadas."],[664,"**Revisões e mensagens de commit** a partir das suas alterações preparadas\nou não commitadas."],[16,"**Route** each file to the deepest partition containing it\n(`PartitionMap::resolve`)."],[428,"**Route** each file to the deepest partition containing it\n(`PartitionMap::resolve`)."],[28,"**Router**: a single actor task owns all state, so routing is lock-free.\nDelivery uses bounded queues and `try_send`: a slow client loses events (and\nis logged) rather than stalling everyone."],[440,"**Router**: a single actor task owns all state, so routing is lock-free.\nDelivery uses bounded queues and `try_send`: a slow client loses events (and\nis logged) rather than stalling everyone."],[250,"**Search that understands code.** Functions, classes and sections are\nindexed whole, found by meaning or by name, across every repository."],[227,"**Search.** The Brokspace view (the folded \"B\" in the activity bar) finds\ncode by meaning or by name; click a result to open it."],[29,"**Semantics**: topic patterns (`file:*`), `source` stamped by the bus,\n`system:*` reserved and broadcast, request/reply via `correlation_id` routed\nonly to the requester (a bounded table with a 15 minute TTL)."],[441,"**Semantics**: topic patterns (`file:*`), `source` stamped by the bus,\n`system:*` reserved and broadcast, request/reply via `correlation_id` routed\nonly to the requester (a bounded table with a 15 minute TTL)."],[619,"**Shards e pacotes de skills oficiais**, revisados e versionados."],[666,"**Shards:** pequenos programas que reagem ao seu workspace por meio de um\nbarramento de eventos local e com permissões."],[254,"**Shards:** small programs that react to your workspace through a local,\npermissioned event bus."],[345,"**shows the requested capabilities and asks for consent** (`--yes` to skip in scripts);"],[757,"**shows the requested capabilities and asks for consent** (`--yes` to skip in scripts);"],[253,"**Skills:** 20 built-in workflows for AI (TDD, code review, specs...), and\nyour own in a `SKILL.md`."],[665,"**Skills:** 20 fluxos de trabalho para IA já incluídos (TDD, code review,\nespecificações...) e os seus próprios em um `SKILL.md`."],[17,"**Skip unchanged files** cheaply: same size and mtime as in `files.json` →\nuntouched; otherwise hash the content and compare."],[429,"**Skip unchanged files** cheaply: same size and mtime as in `files.json` →\nuntouched; otherwise hash the content and compare."],[330,"**Smaller is often better** for interactive use: a fast 7B beats a slow\n14B for everyday questions; switch per request with `-p`."],[742,"**Smaller is often better** for interactive use: a fast 7B beats a slow\n14B for everyday questions; switch per request with `-p`."],[329,"**Storage**: keep models on an SSD; loading from a spinning disk is painfully slow."],[741,"**Storage**: keep models on an SSD; loading from a spinning disk is painfully slow."],[26,"**Transport**: Unix domain socket at `.brokspace/run/brok.sock` (falls back\nto `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` for long paths) or the named pipe\n`\\\\.\\pipe\\brok-<hash of the workspace path>`. Frames are a 4-byte big-endian\nlength plus JSON, capped at 16 MiB."],[438,"**Transport**: Unix domain socket at `.brokspace/run/brok.sock` (falls back\nto `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` for long paths) or the named pipe\n`\\\\.\\pipe\\brok-<hash of the workspace path>`. Frames are a 4-byte big-endian\nlength plus JSON, capped at 16 MiB."],[179,"**User-invoked** skills are started by you (type `/name` in your agent, e.g.\n`/grill-me` before a big change). **Model-invoked** skills are picked by the\nagent when the task fits (e.g. `tdd`, `code-review`)."],[591,"**User-invoked** skills are started by you (type `/name` in your agent, e.g.\n`/grill-me` before a big change). **Model-invoked** skills are picked by the\nagent when the task fits (e.g. `tdd`, `code-review`)."],[15,"**Walk** with the `ignore` crate (nested `.gitignore`s, global excludes),\nthen apply `index.include` / `index.exclude`."],[427,"**Walk** with the `ignore` crate (nested `.gitignore`s, global excludes),\nthen apply `index.include` / `index.exclude`."],[121,"**Windows (PowerShell)**"],[533,"**Windows (PowerShell)**"],[20,"**Write**: delete the file's previous chunks, append the new ones, update\nBM25 and the manifest, then commit atomically. Files are processed in\nbatches of 512 so memory stays bounded on large repositories."],[432,"**Write**: delete the file's previous chunks, append the new ones, update\nBM25 and the manifest, then commit atomically. Files are processed in\nbatches of 512 so memory stays bounded on large repositories."],[21,"`brok index` and `brok run` take an exclusive OS file lock on\n`databases/.lock`; readers (`brok search`, `brok status`) never block."],[433,"`brok index` and `brok run` take an exclusive OS file lock on\n`databases/.lock`; readers (`brok search`, `brok status`) never block."],[60,"`brok init` writes `.brokspace/brok.yml` with comments (commands that change\nthe file, like `brok setup llm`, keep them; comments you add yourself are\ndropped when brok rewrites the file). Every key is optional;\nmissing keys take the defaults below. Unknown keys are rejected with a\n\"did you mean\" style error, so typos never go unnoticed."],[472,"`brok init` writes `.brokspace/brok.yml` with comments (commands that change\nthe file, like `brok setup llm`, keep them; comments you add yourself are\ndropped when brok rewrites the file). Every key is optional;\nmissing keys take the defaults below. Unknown keys are rejected with a\n\"did you mean\" style error, so typos never go unnoticed."],[41,"`brok run` is the daemon in the foreground; `brok start` launches the same\nprocess detached (output in `.brokspace/logs/brok.log`), and `brok ask`,\n`chat`, `review`, `commit` and `skill run` start it on demand. Readiness means\nthe bus is listening and, when installed, `brok-agent` is connected; the CLI\nchecks it with a `daemon:status` request."],[453,"`brok run` is the daemon in the foreground; `brok start` launches the same\nprocess detached (output in `.brokspace/logs/brok.log`), and `brok ask`,\n`chat`, `review`, `commit` and `skill run` start it on demand. Readiness means\nthe bus is listening and, when installed, `brok-agent` is connected; the CLI\nchecks it with a `daemon:status` request."],[368,"`brok run` starts the entrypoint with:"],[780,"`brok run` starts the entrypoint with:"],[75,"`brok setup llm` also stores your LLM choice in the user configuration\n(`~/.config/brokspace/config.yml`, `~/Library/Application Support/brokspace/`\nor `%APPDATA%\\brokspace\\`; override with `BROK_CONFIG_DIR`). `brok init`\napplies it to every new workspace, so you choose a model once per machine."],[487,"`brok setup llm` also stores your LLM choice in the user configuration\n(`~/.config/brokspace/config.yml`, `~/Library/Application Support/brokspace/`\nor `%APPDATA%\\brokspace\\`; override with `BROK_CONFIG_DIR`). `brok init`\napplies it to every new workspace, so you choose a model once per machine."],[315,"`brok setup llm` applies exactly this table. Override it any time:"],[727,"`brok setup llm` applies exactly this table. Override it any time:"],[195,"`brok upgrade` downloads the new `brok` and `brok-agent`, checks them\nagainst the release checksums, swaps them in and restarts brok in every\nworkspace where it was running (each workspace's agent is refreshed on\nthat restart). `brok doctor` tells you when a new version is out."],[607,"`brok upgrade` downloads the new `brok` and `brok-agent`, checks them\nagainst the release checksums, swaps them in and restarts brok in every\nworkspace where it was running (each workspace's agent is refreshed on\nthat restart). `brok doctor` tells you when a new version is out."],[401,"`brok` ships a curated set, embedded in the binary (source:\nskills/). They cover the whole development loop that\nBrokspace itself uses: align, specify, slice, build test-first, review, ship."],[813,"`brok` ships a curated set, embedded in the binary (source:\nskills/). They cover the whole development loop that\nBrokspace itself uses: align, specify, slice, build test-first, review, ship."],[383,"`client.context()` returns the workspace root, your `shards.<name>.settings`\nfrom `brok.yml` and the `llm` routing table."],[795,"`client.context()` returns the workspace root, your `shards.<name>.settings`\nfrom `brok.yml` and the `llm` routing table."],[382,"`client.reply(&request, &payload)` answers a request; only the requester\nreceives it."],[794,"`client.reply(&request, &payload)` answers a request; only the requester\nreceives it."],[381,"`client.request(event)` returns a stream of replies; `client.call::<Req,\nRes>(&req, timeout)` waits for the first typed reply. Example: query the\nindex with `client.call::<SearchRequest, SearchResults>(…)` (add\n`index:search` to `publishes_to`)."],[793,"`client.request(event)` returns a stream of replies; `client.call::<Req,\nRes>(&req, timeout)` waits for the first typed reply. Example: query the\nindex with `client.call::<SearchRequest, SearchResults>(…)` (add\n`index:search` to `publishes_to`)."],[53,"`embeddings`"],[465,"`embeddings`"],[88,"`git-lfs` tracks `.brokspace/databases/**` with Git LFS and stops ignoring it,\nso the index travels with the repository. The object storage sync engine\n(`brok sync`) is on the roadmap: today `brok setup sync` records the target."],[500,"`git-lfs` tracks `.brokspace/databases/**` with Git LFS and stops ignoring it,\nso the index travels with the repository. The object storage sync engine\n(`brok sync`) is on the roadmap: today `brok setup sync` records the target."],[52,"`index`"],[464,"`index`"],[56,"`llm`"],[468,"`llm`"],[367,"`namespace:name`, lowercase letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.` for sub-topics:\n`file:changed`, `agent:ask.chunk`. Patterns are exact topics or a prefix\nending in `*` (`agent:ask.*`, `file:*`, `*`). Pick a namespace named after\nyour shard for your own events. The well-known topics and their payloads are\nlisted in Architecture."],[779,"`namespace:name`, lowercase letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.` for sub-topics:\n`file:changed`, `agent:ask.chunk`. Patterns are exact topics or a prefix\nending in `*` (`agent:ask.*`, `file:*`, `*`). Pick a namespace named after\nyour shard for your own events. The well-known topics and their payloads are\nlisted in Architecture."],[55,"`search`"],[467,"`search`"],[334,"`shard.json`"],[746,"`shard.json`"],[409,"`shard.json` of a skill shard:"],[821,"`shard.json` of a skill shard:"],[58,"`shards`"],[470,"`shards`"],[57,"`sync`"],[469,"`sync`"],[51,"`workspace`"],[463,"`workspace`"],[148,"> Your next project is faster: the search model and your LLM choice are\n> remembered, so `brok init` there takes seconds."],[560,"> Your next project is faster: the search m